UPDATE scholarships SET title = 'Universidad Nacional de Colombia - ''UNAL Doctoral Scholarship for International Researchers'' is an invented importer name; UNAL postgraduate awards are an internal system for its own students (retired)', description = 'RETIRED in Pass 123 (2026-10-28) as an invented importer name. There is no "UNAL Doctoral Scholarship for International Researchers": no award of that or any equivalent name exists in the Universidad Nacional de Colombia''s Sistema Nacional de Becas, whose official postgraduate scholarship page was fetched first-hand for this pass (chunks 0 and 5 of 6). What the system actually contains is (a) internal awards - Beca de Posgrado in its Grado de Honor form (automatic admission, total exemption from administrative and academic fees, and 9 legal monthly minimum wages per calendar semester for a specialisation or master, 15 for a health speciality or doctorate, for students who earned the Grado de Honor distinction in a UNAL undergraduate programme), Asistente Docente and Auxiliar Docente teaching awards for enrolled UNAL postgraduate students, and faculty academic-fee exemptions; and (b) external agreements, where third parties fund students already admitted at UNAL (for example the Fundacion Juan Pablo Gutierrez Caceres master''s agreements) alongside outbound mobility items. Every internal award presupposes a UNAL enrolment or UNAL undergraduate transcript; none is an entrance scholarship for an incoming foreign researcher. The surviving record 712 documents that internal system in full. This retired row previously carried an invented 13,000 US dollars and a July 31 annual deadline (removed in the 2026-10-26 decontamination) and then sat as an unverified placeholder at reliability 4; it is now closed rather than rewritten, because the named award does not exist. A foreign candidate can study at UNAL but must arrive funded; no terms from other Colombian channels (for example MinCiencias or ICETEX instruments) are established by this record.', requirements = 'Do not apply on the basis of this record - it is retired and names no real award. For postgraduate funding at the Universidad Nacional de Colombia, see record 712: the internal Sistema Nacional de Becas (Beca de Posgrado Grado de Honor, teaching assistant/auxiliary awards and faculty fee exemptions) is reserved to UNAL''s own enrolled students and graduates. Incoming international students need their own funding before arrival.', deadline = 'Retired - no award of this name exists, so there is no application round. The internal awards that do exist follow per-semester formalisation windows (for 2026-2, the Grado de Honor window ran 15 June-31 July 2026) and are documented in record 712.', deadline_date = NULL, deadline_type = 'not_published', application_status = 'closed', recurrence = 'none', expected_opening_period = NULL, expected_deadline_period = NULL, rounds = '[]', eligible_countries = '["RETIRED - invented importer name; UNAL postgraduate awards form an internal system for UNAL students and graduates (see record 712)"]', funding_type = 'RETIRED - invented importer name; no UNAL doctoral scholarship for international researchers exists', tuition_coverage = NULL, coverage_type = 'Unspecified', award_amount = NULL, award_currency = NULL, award_period = NULL, award_basis = NULL, living_allowance = NULL, travel_allowance = NULL, accommodation = NULL, required_documents = '[]', english_requirements = 'Not applicable - retired record. Teaching at UNAL is in Spanish; see record 712.', website_url = 'https://posgrados.unal.edu.co/becas/', application_url = 'https://posgrados.unal.edu.co/becas/', source_url = 'https://posgrados.unal.edu.co/becas/', verification_status = 'verified', source_reliability = 9, is_active = false, last_verified_at = now(), last_updated_at = now(), notes = 'PASS 123 RETIREMENT 2026-10-28 (Colombia): invented importer name. UNAL''s official postgraduate becas page fetched first-hand today (new source 3138; chunks 0 and 5 of 6 read): the Sistema Nacional de Becas administers internal awards (Posgrado-Grado de Honor with total fee exemption and 9/15 smmlv per calendar semester; Asistente Docente; Auxiliar Docente; Exencion Derechos Academicos) and external agreements (e.g. Fundacion Juan Pablo Gutierrez Caceres master''s support for admitted UNAL students; an outbound A Coruna mobility item). No award for incoming international researchers appears, and every internal line presupposes UNAL enrolment or a UNAL undergraduate record - exactly as the surviving record 712 (rel 8, same university 190, rewritten 2026-10-25 from the same page) already documents, including the 2026-2 formalisation window 15 Jun-31 Jul 2026. This row''s invented USD 13,000 and July 31 deadline were already removed on 2026-10-26; the row then sat at rel 4 as an unverified placeholder with the bare unal.edu.co domain (retained source 835). Disposition: retire as an invented name (do not rewrite into 712''s system - that record exists; do not revive). Catalogue row us 665 deleted; us 178 (record 712) untouched. Source 3138 also linked to 712 to complete the survivor''s audit trail. MinCiencias/ICETEX foreigner channels were not fetched in this pass and nothing about them is asserted. Rel 9; university_id 190 retained.' WHERE id = 403;

-- 3) Retire 404 (real mechanism = UL Young Researchers, employment model; queue for future additions batch)
UPDATE scholarships SET title = 'University of Ljubljana - ''International Doctoral Grant'' is an invented importer name; doctoral funding runs through employed Young Researcher positions (retired)', description = 'RETIRED in Pass 123 (2026-10-28) as an invented importer name. The University of Ljubljana runs no "International Doctoral Grant": its official doctoral-study page, fetched first-hand for this pass, presents doctoral study and its funding without any such award. The real mechanism is the Slovenian young-researcher system, described on the university''s official Young researchers page (also fetched): young researchers are doctoral students EMPLOYED full-time in research programmes at UL member institutions - their doctoral tuition fees are fully covered and their employer provides the material resources for the research. Positions are published as job tenders, not scholarship rounds (in 2026 UL ran a first call, published 16 March with an 8 May deadline, and a second call, published 1 September with a 10 September deadline; both are completed). Application conditions on the fetched page: at most 4 years after completing a second-cycle programme, an average grade of at least 8.00 in the second-cycle programme and final thesis plus the other conditions for election to the title of assistant, no completed doctorate and no previous young-researcher employment; employment requires enrolling in the 1st or 2nd year of a UL doctoral programme, the assistant habilitation title, entry in the ARIS register of researchers and membership of the same research programme as the supervisor. Candidates apply in parallel to the young-researcher tender and to doctoral enrolment in the eVS portal; the page''s FAQ explicitly provides for candidates who completed their studies outside UL and abroad (diploma supplement plus official grade scale). This retired row compounded the invented name with a wrong-institution address: its stored link, ijs.si, belongs to the Jozef Stefan Institute, not the University of Ljubljana (already flagged in the 2026-10-26 decontamination, which removed the importer''s invented 18,000 US dollars and February 28 annual deadline). The young-researcher system itself may be evaluated as a candidate for a future additions batch under its real identity (ARIS-funded employment across Slovenian research organisations, including UL members and the Jozef Stefan Institute); no salary figure, language condition or foreigner term is asserted by this retired record.', requirements = 'Do not apply on the basis of this record - it is retired and names no real award. For funded doctoral study at the University of Ljubljana, the genuine channel is employment as a young researcher in a research programme (full-time job tender plus parallel doctoral enrolment), under the conditions summarised in the description and on the university''s official Young researchers page.', deadline = 'Retired - no grant of this name exists, so there is no application round. Young-researcher positions are published as job tenders (two windows ran at UL in 2026: deadlines 8 May and 10 September, both completed); future windows must be read on the official tender pages.', deadline_date = NULL, deadline_type = 'not_published', application_status = 'closed', recurrence = 'none', expected_opening_period = NULL, expected_deadline_period = NULL, rounds = '[]', eligible_countries = '["RETIRED - invented importer name; funded UL doctorates run through employed Young Researcher positions (see description)"]', funding_type = 'RETIRED - invented importer name; the real instrument is full-time employment as a young researcher with tuition covered', tuition_coverage = NULL, coverage_type = 'Unspecified', award_amount = NULL, award_currency = NULL, award_period = NULL, award_basis = NULL, living_allowance = NULL, travel_allowance = NULL, accommodation = NULL, required_documents = '[]', english_requirements = 'Not applicable - retired record; no language condition for young-researcher employment is asserted here.', website_url = 'https://www.uni-lj.si/en/research/young-researchers', application_url = 'https://www.uni-lj.si/en/research/young-researchers', source_url = 'https://www.uni-lj.si/en/research/young-researchers', verification_status = 'verified', source_reliability = 9, is_active = false, last_verified_at = now(), last_updated_at = now(), notes = 'PASS 123 RETIREMENT 2026-10-28 (Slovenia): invented importer name. First-hand fetches today: UL official Doctoral study page (new source 3140 - no International Doctoral Grant; doctoral funding presented via Young researchers) and UL official Young researchers page (new source 3139, chunk 0 of 2 - employed doctoral students in UL member research programmes; tuition fully covered; employer provides research resources; 2026 calls published 2026-03-16 deadline 2026-05-08 and published 2026-09-01 deadline 2026-09-10, both "Completed", type "Job application"; conditions: within 4 years of second-cycle completion, average grade at least 8.00 plus assistant-election conditions, no completed doctorate, no prior young-researcher employment; employment conditions: enrol in UL doctorate year 1/2 for 2026/27, assistant title, ARIS register, same research programme as supervisor, full-time UL employment, student status throughout; two parallel applications - tender via studij.uni-lj.si/mr and enrolment via eVS; FAQ provides for foreign-degree candidates with diploma supplement and official grade scale). The row''s stored ijs.si link belongs to the Jozef Stefan Institute (a different institution) and its invented USD 18,000 / February 28 terms were already removed on 2026-10-26; importer root source 2651 (ul.uni-lj.si) retained as audit trail. Disposition: retire as an invented name (Pass 122 shape). No university_scholarships row existed. QUEUE (future additions batch, not a rewrite target): evaluate the Slovenian young-researcher (mladi raziskovalci) system as its own record - ARIS-funded employment at research organisations (UL members, Jozef Stefan Institute and others); salary levels, language conditions and the ARIS call structure require first-hand reads and are not asserted here. Rel 9; university_id remains NULL.' WHERE id = 404;

